{:edb/db-before-t 1908 :edb/db-after-t 1909 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535221 50 #inst "2026-10-08T19:52:08.810Z" 13194139535221 true] [17592186198193 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338293 13194139535221 true] [17592186198194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338300 13194139535221 true] [17592186198195 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338307 13194139535221 true] [17592186198195 1020 #edb/ref 17592186338314 13194139535221 true] [17592186198696 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535221 true] [17592186198696 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A = {k ∈ Z: k^{2} + 1 \\le 5}$?" 13194139535221 false] [17592186198696 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A={k\\in Z:{k}^{2}+1\\le 5}?$" 13194139535221 true] [17592186198696 1145 "The elements of the given set are the integers that satisfy the inequality ${k}^{2}+1\\le 5.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}+1 & \\le 5 \\\\ {k}^{2} & \\le 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{{k}^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{4} \\\\ |k| & \\le 2 \\\\ -2\\le k & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integer solutions of the inequality above are $0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2.$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA={0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2}.\n$$" 13194139535221 true] [17592186338293 1017 #edb/ref 17592186338294 13194139535221 true] [17592186338293 1089 "q-181137" 13194139535221 true] [17592186338293 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535221 true] [17592186338293 1100 "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:{x}^{2}+1=0}?$" 13194139535221 true] [17592186338293 1113 #uuid "aebc17a9-1c9a-5a0d-b525-dec4f8fd7314" 13194139535221 true] [17592186338293 1145 "The elements of the given set are the real numbers that satisfy the equation ${x}^{2}+1=0.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-1} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, since $x\\in R$ and $\\pm \\text{i}\\notin R,$ we conclude that the set $A$ contains no elements. Hence, $A=∅.$" 13194139535221 true] [17592186338294 1000 